From 271f9c88bbdfd51af0c3cf8626a40c0e04f461c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vortiago <atle@havso.net>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 09:17:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] moe: split the routed experts of a prefill ubatch between the
 card and the CPU

The gpu backend keeps every expert in RAM and runs them on the CPU (op
offload off), because uploading nearly all experts per ubatch over PCIe
gen3 x8 was slower. In a real 512-token ubatch about 43 experts a layer
get 32 or more tokens and carry half of the routed rows.

LLAMA_MOE_SPLIT=<n>: per layer, the experts with at least n tokens of the
ubatch (at most LLAMA_MOE_SPLIT_MAX, default 64) are uploaded to a small
buffer on the card and computed there, from a helper thread on its own
backend instance, while the CPU computes the rest. A negative id in a CPU
MUL_MAT_ID now means: another backend computes this row, the row is zero.
With GGML_CUDA_REGISTER_HOST set, the expert memory (the file mmap) is
registered as pinned, so the uploads run without the CPU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C6MCJC4HTKxvuGjKjqDuqQ
